<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Grant is a 62-year-old man who asked for a same-day visit. Last week the otolaryngologist biopsied an ulcerated lesion of his right tonsillar pillar, and pathology showed p16-negative squamous cell carcinoma. Staging PET/CT is booked for two days from now. He stopped cigars two weeks ago and takes varenicline 1 mg twice daily. Three days ago he developed a runny nose and sneezing, followed by a dry cough. His highest home temperature was 37.8 °C. Several people at a meeting he attended last week have had colds. Home COVID-19 antigen tests on the first and third days were negative. Coughing fits make his right-sided throat pain worse, now 6 of 10, up from 5 last week. He uses the lidocaine rinse before meals and the acetaminophen solution 20 mL up to four times a day. He has taken no other medicines, because he was unsure what was safe. He is still managing soft foods and two supplement drinks a day, and he has not choked or coughed while eating or drinking. His saliva was streaked with blood the day after the biopsy and has been clear since. The urge for a cigar is stronger when he coughs, but he has not smoked. He worries that the cough means the cancer has spread to his lungs. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Onset</td><td>Three days ago</td></tr><tr><td>Location</td><td>Nose, throat, and chest</td></tr><tr><td>Duration</td><td>Three days</td></tr><tr><td>Character</td><td>Dry cough; clear nasal discharge; sneezing</td></tr><tr><td>Severity</td><td>Moderate; coughing raises his throat pain from 5 to 6 of 10</td></tr><tr><td>Timing</td><td>Cough worse at night and on waking</td></tr><tr><td>Context</td><td>Colds among people at a meeting last week; one week after tonsil biopsy; two weeks after stopping cigars</td></tr><tr><td>Modifying factors</td><td>Warm drinks and honey help; lidocaine rinse before meals</td></tr><tr><td>Associated signs and symptoms</td><td>Fatigue. Denies sputum, hemoptysis, breathlessness, chest pain, choking or coughing with swallowing, and fever above 37.8 °C</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

